    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41996" root="وصد" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِصَادٌ</span></b>  (M, L,) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِصَادٌ</span>, (L,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَصِيدٌ</span></b> 
[see the Kur, xviii. 17,] (K,) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مطبق</span>: (M,
L, K.:) [in a copy of the M written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَطْبَقٌ</span>: in
the L, without any syll. signs: in the CK,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُطْبَق</span>: and in my MS. copy of the K, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُطْبِق</span>:
see the remarks on these words in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصد</span>:]) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِصَادٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِصَادٌ</span> are like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طِبَاقٌ</span>. (O.)

